    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Modern pattern</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Walmart</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Amazon</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Dependency Injection &amp; Inversion of Control</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Stop letting classes build their own collaborators. Hand them in through the constructor, wire everything in one place, and swap real parts for fakes in tests. Learn constructor vs setter injection, manual wiring in <code>main</code>, why a service locator is not the same thing, how <code>ServiceLoader</code> discovers plug-ins, and what Spring actually does for you.</p>\r\n"
  },
